factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script says the mocchai crop is 'முழுவதுமாக பாதிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளது' (completely damaged), but the article says the wild animals damage the crop and yields are cut by half or more, not wholly destroyed; the article's 'முழுவதுமாக' applies to the season being affected, which the draft misattributes to the crop.
  The reel_script says the yield was 'பாதிக்குமேல் கிடைக்காது' in the slides, but the reel_script's statement that the yield dropped from 700 kg to 200 kg over two years is mixed with the current-season wild boar damage in the same passage, combining two different causes (drought and wild animals) into one sentence.
  The reel_script states that 'இந்த ஆண்டு மழை கிடைத்தும் வனவிலங்குகள் பயிரை சூறையாடுகின்றன' only in the caption, but the reel_script omits the 'சீமைகருவேல மரங்கள் செழித்து வளர்ந்துள்ளன' near Thirumoorthy hill as a cause of the wild boar presence, which is an important cause stated in the article.
  The reel_script omits the key fact that the farmers spent about 25,000 rupees per acre on cultivation, and the article's point that the yield loss affects their livelihood (வாழ்வாதாரம்) is not conveyed.
  The caption and slides say the farmers 'விதைத்து 40 நாட்களான' condition with 10 acres damaged 'நாள்தோறும்'; the slides say 'ஆயிரக்கணக்கான ஏக்கரில் மானாவாரியாக பயிரிடப்படுகிறது', which is accurate, but the slides list 'முள்ளம்பன்றிகள்' as attacking, which the article supports, so no issue there.
